## Proof

The characteristic function $\chi(t) = e^{-|t|^{1.9}}$ is that of a **symmetric stable distribution** with index of stability $\alpha = 1.9 \in (0,2]$.

**Key property of stable laws.** If $X_1, \dots, X_n$ are i.i.d. with characteristic function $e^{-|t|^\alpha}$, then $S_n = X_1+\cdots+X_n$ has characteristic function
$$
\mathbb{E}\,e^{itS_n} = \prod_{k=1}^n e^{-|t|^\alpha} = e^{-n|t|^\alpha}.
$$
Consequently, for $n^{-1/\alpha}S_n$,
$$
\mathbb{E}\,e^{it\,n^{-1/\alpha}S_n} = e^{-n\,|t\,n^{-1/\alpha}|^\alpha} = e^{-n\cdot n^{-1}|t|^\alpha} = e^{-|t|^\alpha}.
$$
So $n^{-1/\alpha}S_n$ has **exactly** the same distribution as $X_1$ for every $n$ (in particular it is tight and non-degenerate).

**Compare the requested scaling with the stable scaling.** Here $\alpha = 1.9 = 19/10$, so
$$
\frac{1}{\alpha} = \frac{10}{19}.
$$
The problem asks for $n^{-5/9}S_n$. Write
$$
n^{-5/9}S_n = n^{\,1/\alpha - 5/9}\cdot\bigl(n^{-1/\alpha}S_n\bigr).
$$
Compute the exponent:
$$
\frac{1}{\alpha} - \frac{5}{9} = \frac{10}{19} - \frac{5}{9} = \frac{90 - 95}{171} = -\frac{5}{171} < 0.
$$
Therefore
$$
n^{\,1/\alpha - 5/9} = n^{-5/171} \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{} 0.
$$

**Convergence to a point mass.** The factor $n^{-1/\alpha}S_n$ is distributed as $X_1$ for all $n$, hence its family of distributions is tight (in fact constant). Multiplying a tight family by a deterministic constant tending to $0$ forces convergence in probability to $0$: for every $\varepsilon > 0$,
$$
\mathbb{P}\bigl(|n^{-5/9}S_n| > \varepsilon\bigr)
= \mathbb{P}\bigl(n^{-1/\alpha}|S_n| > \varepsilon\, n^{5/9-1/\alpha}\bigr)
= \mathbb{P}\bigl(|X_1| > \varepsilon\, n^{5/171}\bigr) \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{} 0,
$$
since $n^{5/171}\to\infty$ and $X_1$ is a.s. finite. Convergence in probability implies weak convergence.

**Conclusion.** The weak limit of $n^{-5/9}S_n$ as $n\to\infty$ is the **degenerate distribution concentrated at $0$**:
$$
n^{-5/9}S_n \xRightarrow{\,d\,} \delta_0.
$$

(Intuitively: $5/9 > 1/\alpha = 10/19$, so we are scaling down by a power *larger* than the natural stable scaling $1/\alpha$; the extra factor $n^{-(5/9-1/\alpha)} = n^{-5/171}$ drives the non-degenerate stable law to $0$.)

